    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (the project's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, with both cases green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature for owners so that a supplied date is preserved and an omitted one defaults to the server's current date, returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges, each kept in its natural home:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf` on `OwnerFields`, this single addition flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`). MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions (no mapper edits needed), and Jackson serializes the `LocalDate` as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field with a `registration_date DATE` column, standard accessors, and a `@PrePersist` callback that defaults it to `LocalDate.now()` only when unset. This is the idiomatic JPA place for a creation-time default: it fires only on insert (so updates never reset it) and never overrides a client-supplied value, keeping the controller/service untouched.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Existing `data.sql` inserts use explicit column lists, so they're unaffected.\n\nBoth acceptance tests \u2014 `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` \u2014 pass.",
